REMARK   3 OTHER DETAILS:                                                       
REMARK   3 KLH1 IS A CYLINDRICAL 8 MDA PROTEIN WITH D5 SYMMETRY AND             
REMARK   3 COMPOSED OF 20 IDENTICAL 400 KDA POLYPEPTIDE SUBUNITS.               
REMARK   3 THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT IS A SUBUNIT DIMER (800 KDA). THE TWO            
REMARK   3 CONSTITUENT POLYPEPTIDES ARE REPRESENTED HERE BY FOUR                
REMARK   3 CHAINS (A, B, C, D). THIS ALLOWS A QUICK VISUALIZATION OF            
REMARK   3 TWO ALTERNATIVE SUBUNIT PATHWAYS THAT HAVE BEEN PROPOSED:            
REMARK   3 A-B + C-D (THIS STUDY) AND A-D + C-B (PDB-ID 3J32).                  
REMARK   3                                                                      
REMARK   3 THE 400 KDA POLYPEPTIDE IS FOLDED INTO EIGHT FUNCTIONAL              
REMARK   3 UNITS, TERMED KLH1-A TO KLH1-H (1-421, 422-835, 836-1255,            
REMARK   3 1256-1664, 1665-2081, 2082-2488, 2489-2905, 2906-3398).              
REMARK   3 THEY ARE CONCATENATED VIA LONG LINKERS. FOR THIS MODEL,              
REMARK   3 THE STRUCTURE OF KLH1-H WAS AVAILABLE (PDB-ID 3QJO).                 
REMARK   3 HOMOLOGY MODELING OF THE OTHER FUNCTIONAL UNITS WAS DONE             
REMARK   3 USING PDB-ID 1JS8 AS TEMPLATE.                                       
REMARK   3                                                                      
REMARK   3 EACH FUNCTIONAL UNIT IS ABLE TO BIND A DIOXYGEN MOLECULE             
REMARK   3 BETWEEN TWO COPPER IONS COORDINATED BY SIX HISTIDINES:               
REMARK   3 42, 60, 69, 179, 183, 210; 462, 482, 491, 602, 606, 633;             
REMARK   3 876, 896, 905, 1015, 1019, 1046; 1293, 1311, 1320, 1424,             
REMARK   3 1428, 1455; 1705, 1725, 1734, 1847, 1851, 1878; 2122,                
REMARK   3 2141, 2150, 2260, 2264, 2291; 2542, 2561, 2570, 2670,                
REMARK   3 2674, 2701; 2946, 2965, 2974, 3075, 3079, 3106.                      
REMARK   3                                                                      
REMARK   3 SUBMISSION BASED ON EXPERIMENTAL DATA FROM EMDB EMD-1569.            
REMARK   3 (DEPOSITION ID: 6428).                                               
